# WhatsApp icon — locked brand glyph

**Canonical asset:** `public/brand-icons/whatsapp.png`  
(Source upload: green speech-bubble mark, white handset, white outer stroke — official WhatsApp lockup.)

## Hard rule

Whenever a WhatsApp affordance appears (CTA, secondary action, share sheet, SRP/PDP contact row, Figma or code):

- **Always** use this exact glyph (or a lossless export of the same lockup).
- **Never** substitute Bricks Iconography `WhatsappLogo` / stroke icons, purple-tinted vectors, generic chat bubbles, or Iconify/Phosphor WhatsApp variants.
- **Never** recolor it with `icon/brand_1`, `surface/brand`, or any Bricks purple — WhatsApp keeps its **brand green + white** lockup.
- Do not redraw or “approximate” the mark. If a new size is needed, scale this asset (or export from the same master), don’t invent paths.

## Usage notes

- Prefer the PNG as an **image fill** / `<img>` / icon component wrapping this file.
- Button chrome around it still uses Bricks tokens (`border/*`, `surface/*`, radius, spacing). Only the **glyph** is exempt from `icon/*` recoloring.
- Product WhatsApp CTA chrome recipe (size/fill/stroke/radius): see `figma-button-chrome` — **`border/brand`**, not `border/default` / `surface/brand` stroke.
- Exception to `bricks-iconography-source` and `bricks-ds-icon-colors` **for WhatsApp only**. All other icons stay on Bricks Iconography + `icon/*` / `semantic_icons/*`.

## Figma / figma-cli

Place via `createImage` / image fill from `public/brand-icons/whatsapp.png` (bytes → `figma.createImage`). Do not instance a Bricks WhatsApp vector for product CTAs.
